course: dictionary
lesson: 11427
title: Acquisition: getting something new
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An acquisition is something you have got or bought, especially something new and valuable. «The museum's new acquisition is a painting from 1800.» The painting is new to the museum, so acquisition means a new item they have got.
explain: The word can also mean the act of getting something. «Her acquisition of a second language took three years.» The words around it tell you what is being got: a second language. Ask yourself, what is the acquisition of? Then swap in the meaning: getting. Does the sentence still make sense? It does.
explain: In business news, acquisition has a special meaning. «One company made an acquisition of its rival.» A company doing something to another company usually means buying it. So this means one company bought another.
fact: An acquisition is something you have got or bought, often something new and valuable.
fact: Language acquisition means how children learn a language.
fact: In business, an acquisition is when one company buys another company.
fact: Useful phrases: a new acquisition, the acquisition of, language acquisition.
exercise: «The library has a new acquisition: a book of old maps.» What is a new acquisition here? | *Something the library has got | A date when the library opened | A room for quiet reading | A person who works in the library
exercise: In school we learn about language acquisition. What does it mean? | A type of school bag | The place where books are kept | *How children learn a language | A test for spelling
exercise: «One firm's acquisition of another firm changed the town's shops.» What does acquisition mean in business news? | *When one company buys another | When a firm moves to a new town | When a company closes down | When a company makes a new logo
test: «Her acquisition of a bike meant she could ride to school.» What was acquired? | A road | *A bike | A school
test: «The acquisition of knowledge takes time and practice.» What does acquisition mean here? | *The act of getting knowledge | A school subject | A book of facts | A loss of knowledge
exam: «The museum's latest acquisition is a bronze statue, bought last spring.» What is a museum acquisition? | A visitor's ticket | A museum guard | *A new item the museum has got | A closed exhibition
